SwiftPutty local patch 0004
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; suitable for upstreaming

terminal.c: free the last-selected-text buffers in term_free().

When a selection is copied to CLIP_LOCAL, clipme() hands its text,
attribute and colour buffers to the Terminal (last_selected_text,
last_selected_attr, last_selected_tc), freeing the previous ones. Nothing
freed the final set: term_free() did not. Upstream frontends free a
Terminal only as their process exits, so it went unnoticed; SwiftPutty
frees one per closed session. Found by `leaks --atExit`.

--- a/terminal/terminal.c
+++ b/terminal/terminal.c
@@ -2131,6 +2131,9 @@
         printer_finish_job(term->print_job);
     bufchain_clear(&term->printer_buf);
     sfree(term->paste_buffer);
+    sfree(term->last_selected_text);
+    sfree(term->last_selected_attr);
+    sfree(term->last_selected_tc);
     sfree(term->ltemp);
     sfree(term->wcFrom);
     sfree(term->wcTo);
